So I have this samurai that's doing fairly well -- level 13, armor
plus protection at -15.  Unfortunately, he has neither levitation or
magic resistance.

Level 13 means that he can't do the quest yet.  

Lack of magic resistance means that the castle level is awfully
dangerous -- lots of liches there. Also no musical instrument, which
means the only way into the front part of the castle is by finding a
wand of striking (which he doesn't have either, currently) and
destroying it. 

Lack of levitation means that taking the back route into the castle
and picking up the goodies guarded by the dragons (which he could
otherwise take on) isn't possible. (No jumping boots, either.)

He does have water walking boots and reflection (the statue of Perseus
at the Medusa level yielded a silver shield but no levitation boots).

I tried taking him down to the Valley of the Dead to try getting one
more level, either though killing things or killing and eating a
wraith. Unfortunately, he kept losing levels and barely regaining them
(damned vampires, and his cloak is displacement, which is MC2, not
MC3), so gave up on that plan.

Anyone have a better suggestion than trying that again?  (There's no
Ludios in this dungeon, best I can tell.)



